---
title: Matcha white chocolate frosting
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W47XPObAgI4
cuisine: Japanese
---

In a #bowl combine @white chocolate{100 g} and @heavy cream{100 g}. Heat in the microwave for ~{30 seconds} until melted and smooth.

In a seperate #bowl, heat up @heavy cream{40 g} until about !60C. Mix with @matcha powder{10 g} until a paste is formed.

Mix the matcha paste into the melted white chocolate and stir until smooth.  Stir in @heavy cream{250 g}.

Cover the frosting with #plastic wrap{} and chill in the freezer for ~{40 minutes} until thickened.

Once thickened, whip the frosting on high speed for ~{5 minutes} until light and fluffy.
